7905 | Page 247 | {} | 2PM  N. Y. May 10th  / New York May 10th for Wm E / Chandler Soliator Navy Dep Washn enquire / of RC Johnson and company / hardware dealers Washn where Jos L / Savage can now be found in / N. Y. & where his books and  / papers are = district attorney wants / to see him forthwith answer / <deletion>Special Commissioner</deletion> / HS Oleutt / Special Commissioner /  /  / 3pm  Manchester Va May 10th 65 / 10th 12 M Lt Gen Grant Your  / dispatch directing me to march / my command to Alexandria just recvd / I have ordered the army of / Ga to move tomorrow and the / Army of Tenn will follow next day / W. T. Sherman / M Genl /  /  / 3 pm  Richmond Va May 10th 1865  / 1230 pm 10th for Hon CA Dana  / your telegraph for the arrest of / Wm Boulware has been received / and orders accordingly  HW Halleck / M Genl / 
8728 | Page 250 | {} | 2.15 pm / To Capt Clowry St Louis  Richmond Va May 13th 1865 / Richmond 1130 am 13th Maj Genl Pope St Louis . / About the first of January 1862  a / prominent gentleman was arrested in St Louis on suspicion / of instigating the destruction of RR bridges . boxes / of cards were found in his house like those / thrown from the cars at the time . His wife was / I think a Miss Pratt . He broke his / parole & escaped to Prices Army his name / I do not remember . There is a Thomas / L Snead here a confederate member of Congress from / Missouri suspected of being the same man . please / ascertain & answer . Col Farrar former Provost Marshal can  / I think inform you . HW Halleck / MG /  /  / 230 pm  Richmond Va May 13th 1865 / 11 am 13th Lt Gen Grant . Have just / learned that the Sanders papers and books / of Orange RR Co have been secured / and are on the way in . / Boulware has been captured and will be sent / immediately to Wash HW Halleck / M Gen / 
